			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1715476">
									

<p>High-birth rate: SCP-1294 reproduces via infecting foxes, causing them to essentially give birth to fungal trees, while SCP-367 reproduces via mitosis.</p>
<p>Can consume massive amounts of material: SCP-1294 can only eat meat in this way, which is a VERY rare event which can pretty much only happen if it encounters a beached blue whale&#8230; in the Sahara. SCP-367 can eat everything, which plays more into its file.</p>
<p>Something that is something else: Yes, but that’s like, an eighth of every animal SCP ever made. If you’re talking about it being the same thing, I could point you to several SCPs that resemble cute animals.</p>

